    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5847" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">būnĭăs</span></b> ,
			ădis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουνιάς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a kind of Swedish turnip</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 10,
				422</span></i>; acc. buniada, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 4,
				11, § 21</span></i>.—Another kind is called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">būnĭon</span></b> ,
				ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βούνιον</span>, Plin. l. l.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">būnītus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>made from
				bunion</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 4, 3, 52</span></i>
			.</div>
